interconnect: qcom: add the SM6375 NoC driver

SM6375 (holi) has the RPM-based NoC layout of QCM2290: BIMC, CNOC,
SNOC and the virtual QUP, MMRT and MMNRT NoCs, with an extra hop for
the multimedia masters through SNOC. Mainline has no driver for it, so
rpmcc hands the bus clocks over at INT_MAX and nothing ever lowers them.

The node data (bus widths, channels, RPM master and slave ids, links)
is from the downstream holi driver of the Xiaomi sunstone-u-oss kernel
(drivers/interconnect/qcom/holi.c), the bus clocks and the AB
coefficients (qcom,util-factor) from its DT. QoS is not programmed: the
boot firmware's settings stay.

Tested on SM4375 (Xiaomi Redmi Note 12 5G).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/Kconfig b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/Kconfig
index b3187acf9..e6cc8f417 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/Kconfig
@@ -358,6 +358,16 @@ config INTERCONNECT_QCOM_SM6115
 	  This is a driver for the Qualcomm Network-on-Chip on sm6115-based
 	  platforms.
 
+config INTERCONNECT_QCOM_SM6375
+	tristate "Qualcomm SM6375 interconnect driver"
+	depends on INTERCONNECT_QCOM
+	depends on QCOM_SMD_RPM
+	depends on ARM64 || COMPILE_TEST
+	select INTERCONNECT_QCOM_SMD_RPM
+	help
+	  This is a driver for the Qualcomm Network-on-Chip on sm6375-based
+	  platforms.
+
 config INTERCONNECT_QCOM_SM6350
 	tristate "Qualcomm SM6350 interconnect driver"
 	depends on INTERCONNECT_QCOM_RPMH_POSSIBLE
